   check-config test and display staged firewall rules
   reload       test and apply staged firewall rules
nsh(config)#
.Ed
.Pp
.Ic pf edit
.Pp
Edit the candidate's firewall rules.
.Nm
gets the rules from
.Xr nshd 8 ,
opens them in the editor that VISUAL or EDITOR names, and sends them
back.
The edit also adds
.Cm pf reload
to the candidate.
.Xr pfctl 8
tests the rules at
.Cm commit
and
.Cm commit check ,
not as the editor exits, and the rules take effect when
.Cm commit
succeeds.
For packet filter configuration syntax, refer to
.Xr pf.conf 5 .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nsh> !man pf.conf
nsh(config)# pf edit
nsh(config)# commit
.Ed
.Pp
.Ic pf check-config
.Pp
Test, with
.Xr pfctl 8 ,
the firewall rules that the last
.Cm commit
wrote, and display them in order with their rule numbers.
If the rules fail the test, the numbers of the lines with errors are
listed.
.Pp
.Ic pf reload
.Pp
Load, with
.Xr pfctl 8 ,
the firewall rules that the last
.Cm commit
wrote.
It does not load the candidate's rules;
.Cm commit
does that.
.Cm pf check-config
and
.Cm pf reload
are operations, which need the operate permission.
